; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Nets of Solids
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     3d, nets, cube, pyramid, tetrahedron, prism
; SUMMARY:  Draws the flat paper patterns that fold up into a cube, a tetrahedron, a square pyramid and a prism.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A net is what a box looks like when you cut it open and lay it
;   flat. Four nets appear, each in its own color, with its name and
;   the number of faces. Print the screen, cut round the outside,
;   fold along the lines, and they really make the solids.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Each net is a procedure with a size input, so you can
;   try  clearscreen pyramidnet 120  in the command center.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * turning LEFT draws a shape on the other side of a line
;   * attaching a shape to every side of another shape with REPEAT
;   * reusing small procedures (SQ, TRI, RECT) to build bigger ones
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * A cube has 11 different nets. Change CUBENET to draw another.
;   * Make a pentagonal pyramid: a pentagon with 5 triangles round it.
;   * Two squares and four rectangles make a cuboid. Draw its net.
; ============================================================

; The basic pieces. They all walk with RIGHT turns and come back
; to where they started, facing the same way.
to sq :s
  repeat 4 [forward :s right 90]
end

to rect :w :h
  repeat 2 [forward :h right 90 forward :w right 90]
end

; An equilateral triangle that sits on the turtle's LEFT side.
; We will glue these onto the edges of shapes drawn with right turns,
; so they always point outwards.
to outtri :s :color
  filled :color [repeat 3 [forward :s left 120]]
end

; Six squares in a cross. We place each square by grid column and row.
to cubenet :s
  localmake "x xcor localmake "y ycor
  foreach [[1 0] [0 1] [1 1] [2 1] [3 1] [1 2]] [
    penup setxy :x + :s * first ? :y + :s * last ? setheading 0 pendown
    filled [255 200 200] [sq :s]
  ]
end

; One triangle with a triangle glued to each of its three sides:
; that is four triangles, which fold up into a tetrahedron.
to tetranet :s
  right 30
  filled [255 230 160] [repeat 3 [forward :s right 120]]
  repeat 3 [outtri :s [255 230 160] forward :s right 120]
  left 30
end

; A square base with a triangle on every side.
to pyramidnet :s
  filled [200 235 200] [sq :s]
  repeat 4 [outtri :s [200 235 200] forward :s right 90]
end

; Three rectangles in a row for the sides, and a triangle on the top
; and the bottom of the middle one for the two ends.
to prismnet :w :h
  localmake "x xcor localmake "y ycor
  repeat 3 [
    penup setxy :x + :w * (repcount - 1) :y setheading 0 pendown
    filled [200 215 255] [rect :w :h]
  ]
  ; bottom triangle: walk along the bottom edge of the middle rectangle
  ; heading left to right, the outward side is on the turtle's right,
  ; so we walk it from right to left instead
  penup setxy :x + 2 * :w :y setheading 270 pendown
  outtri :w [200 215 255]
  ; top triangle: along the top edge from left to right
  penup setxy :x + :w :y + :h setheading 90 pendown
  outtri :w [200 215 255]
end

to caption :x :y :text
  penup setxy :x :y setpencolor [60 60 60]
  label :text
  setpencolor [40 40 40]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setpensize 2
setpencolor [40 40 40]
setlabelheight 15

penup setxy -370 70 pendown
cubenet 50
caption -360 30 [Cube: 6 squares]

penup setxy 110 120 setheading 0 pendown
tetranet 90
caption 100 15 [Tetrahedron: 4 triangles]

penup setxy -260 -200 setheading 0 pendown
pyramidnet 70
caption -330 -280 [Square pyramid: 1 square, 4 triangles]

penup setxy 120 -190 setheading 0 pendown
prismnet 60 110
caption 80 -280 [Prism: 3 rectangles, 2 triangles]
